size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        // Simple token-by-token comparison
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        return max_idx;
    }

    // Multimodal path
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai =   tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
            // Both are multimodal placeholders - compare by chunk ID
            const auto & a_chunk =   find_chunk(i);
            const auto & b_chunk = b.find_chunk(i);
            GGML_ASSERT(a_chunk && b_chunk);

            const std::string id_ai = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(a_chunk.get());
            const std::string id_bi = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(b_chunk.get());

            const size_t n_tok_a = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(a_chunk.get());
            const size_t n_tok_b = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(b_chunk.get());

            if (id_ai == id_bi && n_tok_a == n_tok_b) {
                // Same chunk - skip over all its tokens
                i += n_tok_a - 1;
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }

        if (ai == bi) {
            continue;
        }
        return i;
    }

    return max_idx;
}
```

So the multimodal path handles cases where both tokens are `LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL` placeholders. When that happens, it retrieves the actual chunk objects and compares their IDs and token counts. If they match, it advances past all the tokens in that chunk. Otherwise, it returns the current position as the divergence point. For regular tokens, it just does a straightforward equality check. The key insight is that when chunks match, the loop increment combined with the manual `i += n_tok_a - 1` adjustment ensures we skip the entire multimodal token sequence correctly. This handles the case where a chunk produces multiple tokens that need to be treated as a single unit for prefix comparison purposes.
